StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": "4728bcf71efd2f460722564132ecab5f3259bc48", "git_parents": ["27b976ad7f1bf1e64a9ca426621b9183015b7e00"], "node": "c15563ac36ebb43baa4256b7be31694581798b64", "parents": ["36bfa64751c13b0dbd4e67ad6c0da04cadee4242"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758804679, "git_changesets": ["4728bcf71efd2f460722564132ecab5f3259bc48"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "242": {"changesets": [{"author": "Karl Tomlinson \u003ckarlt+@karlt.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988931 use GetInstanceIfExists() from MediaTrackGraphImpl::GetInstance()  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265213\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265876\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "11829818fa939aa610972af61e80cd25a6b6b6e5", "git_parents": ["4728bcf71efd2f460722564132ecab5f3259bc48"], "node": "18789f17f2fee079cd2886dd6ff7e0f95fbe4e6b", "parents": ["c15563ac36ebb43baa4256b7be31694581798b64"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758804738, "git_changesets": ["11829818fa939aa610972af61e80cd25a6b6b6e5"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "243": {"changesets": [{"author": "William Durand \u003cwill+git@drnd.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1989205 - Update recommended.xpi file to fix a test (permafailure) for ESR. r=robwu a=dmeehan DONTBUILD\n\nThe new XPI file has been generated from this PR [1], and signed by the\nAMO -dev instance (which uses the nonprod cert). FTR since this add-on\nneeds a recommendation state, we must add the add-on to the \"By Firefox\"\npromoted group via the AMO admin before getting the version signed.\n\nBefore:\n\n```\n$ xpidump old.xpi\nMANIFEST:\n  ID        : N/A\n  Version   : 2.0\n  Enterprise: No\n\nRECOMMENDATION:\n  [Line]\n\nSIGNATURES:\n  PKCS7:\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 PRESENT / PRODUCTION / SHA-1 / REGULAR ADD-ON\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 Certificates:\n\t\u2514\u2500\u2500 Common Name         (CN): signingca1.addons.mozilla.org\n\t    Organizational Unit (OU): Mozilla AMO Production Signing Service\n\t    End Date                : 2025-04-04T00:00:00Z\n\t\u2514\u2500\u2500 Common Name         (CN): {811d77f1-f306-4187-9251-b4ff99bad60b}\n\t    Organizational Unit (OU): Production\n\t    End Date                : 2030-09-15T16:50:45Z\n  COSE:\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 PRESENT / PRODUCTION / ES256 / REGULAR ADD-ON\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 Certificates:\n\t\u2514\u2500\u2500 Common Name         (CN): signingca1.addons.mozilla.org\n\t    Organizational Unit (OU): Mozilla AMO Production Signing Service\n\t    End Date                : 2025-04-04T00:00:00Z\n\t\u2514\u2500\u2500 Common Name         (CN): {811d77f1-f306-4187-9251-b4ff99bad60b}\n\t    Organizational Unit (OU): Production\n\t    End Date                : 2030-09-15T16:50:45Z\n```\n\nAfter:\n\n```\n$ xpidump new.xpi\nMANIFEST:\n  ID        : recommended-line@test.mozilla.org\n  Version   : 3.0\n  Enterprise: No\n\nRECOMMENDATION:\n  [Line]\n\nSIGNATURES:\n  PKCS7:\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 PRESENT / STAGING / SHA-256 / REGULAR ADD-ON\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 Certificates:\n\t\u2514\u2500\u2500 Common Name         (CN): cas-intermediate-amo-ca-staging\n\t    Organizational Unit (OU): Mozilla Staging Signing Service\n\t    End Date                : 2050-12-31T00:00:00Z\n\t\u2514\u2500\u2500 Common Name         (CN): recommended-line@test.mozilla.org\n\t    Organizational Unit (OU): Production\n\t    End Date                : 2035-09-17T07:29:49Z\n  COSE:\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 PRESENT / STAGING / ES256 / REGULAR ADD-ON\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 Certificates:\n\t\u2514\u2500\u2500 Common Name         (CN): cas-intermediate-amo-ca-staging\n\t    Organizational Unit (OU): Mozilla Staging Signing Service\n\t    End Date                : 2050-12-31T00:00:00Z\n\t\u2514\u2500\u2500 Common Name         (CN): recommended-line@test.mozilla.org\n\t    Organizational Unit (OU): Production\n\t    End Date                : 2035-09-17T07:29:49Z\n```\n\n[1]: https://github.com/mozilla/mozilla-central-test-xpis/pull/15\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265576\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpinstall/browser_doorhanger_installs.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpinstall/recommended.xpi"], "git_node": "6f08eaa1883760f1deb3ade92888cc92b430d257", "git_parents": ["11829818fa939aa610972af61e80cd25a6b6b6e5"], "node": "38d1ea89c6642e4639f9894c0a66b7f715cdf126", "parents": ["18789f17f2fee079cd2886dd6ff7e0f95fbe4e6b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758805292, "git_changesets": ["6f08eaa1883760f1deb3ade92888cc92b430d257"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "244": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988114. r=ahale a=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D264683\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.h"], "git_node": "35523c86dc5aa4130bc913d2f91ae17f4d09c942", "git_parents": ["6f08eaa1883760f1deb3ade92888cc92b430d257"], "node": "568cb03c2004d711986f27be6b4b7c1ef453330b", "parents": ["38d1ea89c6642e4639f9894c0a66b7f715cdf126"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1989517 - Ensure DrawTarget removed from RecordedTextureDestruction playback. r=aosmond, a=dmeehan\n\nCanvasTranslator::RemoveTexture delayed the call to RemoveDrawTarget till all keepalives are\ngone. However, this may take place long after RecordedTextureDestruction actually called\nRemoveTexture. This gives time for subsequent DrawTargets with the same ReferencePtr to be\ncreated, causing the wrong DrawTargets to be removed.\n\nThis patch ensures that when RemoveTexture is called from a RecordedTextureDestruction event\nthat the DrawTarget is always removed then and there, rather than waiting.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265867\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.h"], "git_node": "7ea9fd74e4a5b79a1b5c361cf59286abddf5515b", "git_parents": ["35523c86dc5aa4130bc913d2f91ae17f4d09c942"], "node": "47c40db2c2b135b892f9f64341e8718467caf89d", "parents": ["568cb03c2004d711986f27be6b4b7c1ef453330b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1989945. r=ahale a=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265664\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/DrawTargetWebgl.cpp"], "git_node": "ce0b8a6e422cb18df3a470f02d901f7395d9bfd8", "git_parents": ["7ea9fd74e4a5b79a1b5c361cf59286abddf5515b"], "node": "6f6098be40e13033d4264016aae95a14a36447f2", "parents": ["47c40db2c2b135b892f9f64341e8718467caf89d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758805601, "git_changesets": ["35523c86dc5aa4130bc913d2f91ae17f4d09c942", "7ea9fd74e4a5b79a1b5c361cf59286abddf5515b", "ce0b8a6e422cb18df3a470f02d901f7395d9bfd8"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "245": {"changesets": [{"author": "DonalMe \u003c76789979+DonalMe@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1989517 - Ensure DrawTarget removed from RecordedTextureDestruction playback. r=aosmond, a=dmeehan\" for causing build failures\n\nThis reverts commit 7ea9fd74e4a5b79a1b5c361cf59286abddf5515b.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.h"], "git_node": "a76aca3306159155ba8b1be634c47026f9e82e1a", "git_parents": ["ce0b8a6e422cb18df3a470f02d901f7395d9bfd8"], "node": "cd0435225cc2137a8faeae15375a00fd75fafcea", "parents": ["6f6098be40e13033d4264016aae95a14a36447f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "DonalMe \u003c76789979+DonalMe@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1988114. r=ahale a=dmeehan\" for causing build failues\n\nThis reverts commit 35523c86dc5aa4130bc913d2f91ae17f4d09c942.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.h"], "git_node": "713f5caf2d896a3c479295effa5c3aadb491c918", "git_parents": ["a76aca3306159155ba8b1be634c47026f9e82e1a"], "node": "00d40f684959f34966089238b7a9d59bedfc5e29", "parents": ["cd0435225cc2137a8faeae15375a00fd75fafcea"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758807619, "git_changesets": ["a76aca3306159155ba8b1be634c47026f9e82e1a", "713f5caf2d896a3c479295effa5c3aadb491c918"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "246": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1982003 - Upgrade allocator-api2 to 0.2.21. a=RyanVM\n\nThe issue that made us fork the crate locally was actually fixed\nupstream in 0.2.21.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D264361\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D264536\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "supply-chain/config.toml", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/README.md", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/nightly.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/boxed.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/macros.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/raw_vec.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/unique.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/vec/into_iter.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/vec/mod.rs"], "git_node": "40dc24686f7ef376f16df927b06206313fc1692f", "git_parents": ["713f5caf2d896a3c479295effa5c3aadb491c918"], "node": "4bd5c9a2da137df02d5597bff7143b12fc5ace84", "parents": ["00d40f684959f34966089238b7a9d59bedfc5e29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1982003 - Apply allocator-api2 upstream fix to build with rust 1.89. a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D264362\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D264537\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "supply-chain/config.toml", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/CHANGELOG.md", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/LICENSE-APACHE", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/LICENSE-MIT", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/README.md", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/nightly.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/alloc/global.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/alloc/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/alloc/system.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/boxed.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/macros.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/raw_vec.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/slice.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/unique.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/vec/drain.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/vec/into_iter.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/vec/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/vec/partial_eq.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/vec/set_len_on_drop.rs", "third_party/rust/allocator-api2/src/stable/vec/splice.rs"], "git_node": "94e68b81a7113a39b7515f03173380d87f35a9e9", "git_parents": ["40dc24686f7ef376f16df927b06206313fc1692f"], "node": "bd658f5989582dbf2ed725779d5cfa04b2ce7c18", "parents": ["4bd5c9a2da137df02d5597bff7143b12fc5ace84"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758855507, "git_changesets": ["40dc24686f7ef376f16df927b06206313fc1692f", "94e68b81a7113a39b7515f03173380d87f35a9e9"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "247": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988114. r=gfx-reviewers,ahale,aosmond a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D266194\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.cpp", "gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.h"], "git_node": "509a406228433147df6c2e15099bdacdd377a970", "git_parents": ["94e68b81a7113a39b7515f03173380d87f35a9e9"], "node": "ff159c364945e7211fd265b94fc1291aa86022c4", "parents": ["bd658f5989582dbf2ed725779d5cfa04b2ce7c18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1989517 - Ensure DrawTarget removed from RecordedTextureDestruction playback. r=aosmond, a=RyanVM\n\nCanvasTranslator::RemoveTexture delayed the call to RemoveDrawTarget till all keepalives are\ngone. However, this may take place long after RecordedTextureDestruction actually called\nRemoveTexture. This gives time for subsequent DrawTargets with the same ReferencePtr to be\ncreated, causing the wrong DrawTargets to be removed.\n\nThis patch ensures that when RemoveTexture is called from a RecordedTextureDestruction event\nthat the DrawTarget is always removed then and there, rather than waiting.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265867\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.h"], "git_node": "1d97d5f6f4e2957f0060565be83ea46957108d30", "git_parents": ["509a406228433147df6c2e15099bdacdd377a970"], "node": "8c0aaf1322ca22b925090dfb0c9e3c67fec41bcc", "parents": ["ff159c364945e7211fd265b94fc1291aa86022c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alwu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1989734 - use the index to find the first SPS. r=media-playback-reviewers,karlt a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265908\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/agnostic/bytestreams/H265.cpp"], "git_node": "5467b82c15b7cc49d5a101fbd0a203d8cdc2ed00", "git_parents": ["1d97d5f6f4e2957f0060565be83ea46957108d30"], "node": "fa3b5d8bc94fc29922076ba0404d62bb3b7c2608", "parents": ["8c0aaf1322ca22b925090dfb0c9e3c67fec41bcc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758857102, "git_changesets": ["509a406228433147df6c2e15099bdacdd377a970", "1d97d5f6f4e2957f0060565be83ea46957108d30", "5467b82c15b7cc49d5a101fbd0a203d8cdc2ed00"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "248": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1987806 - Null check compartmentPrivate in FindSameOriginCompartment.  a=RyanVM\n\nWe're hitting some null crashes in CompartmentOriginInfo::IsSameOrigin,\nso maybe this is due to a null compartment private? We're iterating\nover all compartments in a zone during SetNewDocument so maybe there's\nsomething weird to stumble over.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D264335\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D266166\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp"], "git_node": "a8ffb60fd2c5869544d8011eef23469647ae78ff", "git_parents": ["5467b82c15b7cc49d5a101fbd0a203d8cdc2ed00"], "node": "69f83e85fd2713d98e575243656986c625d506b0", "parents": ["fa3b5d8bc94fc29922076ba0404d62bb3b7c2608"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758860190, "git_changesets": ["a8ffb60fd2c5869544d8011eef23469647ae78ff"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "249": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ben Dean-Kawamura \u003cbdk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1989840 - vendor app-services fix,  a=RyanVM\n\n- Updated `Cargo.toml` to point to the app-services commit with the fix\n- Reverted my default rust to `1.86.0`\n- Ran `./mach configure` and `./mach vendor rust`\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D266197\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/webext-storage/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/webext-storage/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "827a745d823b0be4bc6eb0255cbb21316002c451", "git_parents": ["a8ffb60fd2c5869544d8011eef23469647ae78ff"], "node": "749c9205fb7f0d8ce362c52d501f63ffc952e6b8", "parents": ["69f83e85fd2713d98e575243656986c625d506b0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758860721, "git_changesets": ["827a745d823b0be4bc6eb0255cbb21316002c451"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "250": {"changesets": [{"author": "Rob Wu \u003crob@robwu.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1979546 - Replace WaitForMultipleObjects with IOCP in Subprocess  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe current WaitForMultipleObjects-based implementation causes a\ndeadlock if 16 or more processes are spawned, as explained in the bug.\n\nThis patch replaces the use of events and WaitForMultipleObjects with\nI/O Completion Ports (IOCP) as the mechanism to monitor I/O progress\nand process terminations. This is not subject to the\nMAXIMUM_WAIT_OBJECTS (64) limit of WaitForMultipleObjects.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D258968\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D266337\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/native_messaging.toml", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_native_messaging_concurrent.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/subprocess_shared_win.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/subprocess_win.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/subprocess_win.worker.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/test/xpcshell/data_test_child.py", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/test/xpcshell/test_subprocess_child.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "9ad1e615444f68a12919587e3c293757e6b87a05", "git_parents": ["827a745d823b0be4bc6eb0255cbb21316002c451"], "node": "8c4662b634a92f07c56c19e0da170b2d361bf5f3", "parents": ["749c9205fb7f0d8ce362c52d501f63ffc952e6b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rob Wu \u003crob@robwu.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1982950 - Stop polling as soon as process exits  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe patch to bug 1979546 refactored the logic that awaits the process\ntermination. The logic that processes process termination should stop\nthe poll loop() via updatePollEvents(). This did not happen, because\nupdatePollEvents() considered a process alive if it is in\n`io.processes`, but the updatePollEvents() was not called when\n`cleanupProcess` cleared the last reference.\n\nConsequently, the poll loop continued forever if the process's pipes\nclosed before the process.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D261060\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D266338\n", "files": ["toolkit/modules/subprocess/subprocess_win.worker.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/subprocess_worker_common.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/test/xpcshell/data_test_script.py", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/test/xpcshell/test_subprocess_polling.js", "toolkit/modules/subprocess/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "d01e2df6064aae16d9593e7b1612b7ce546e3f6d", "git_parents": ["9ad1e615444f68a12919587e3c293757e6b87a05"], "node": "f8c237a193f7fd480719766064c3f3b67a7bf112", "parents": ["8c4662b634a92f07c56c19e0da170b2d361bf5f3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1758898166, "git_changesets": ["9ad1e615444f68a12919587e3c293757e6b87a05", "d01e2df6064aae16d9593e7b1612b7ce546e3f6d"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "251": {"changesets": [{"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1973699, modernize nsDocShell accesses a bit,  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D265021\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D266239\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDSURIContentListener.cpp", "docshell/b